Spec: specs/001-core-and-anthropic-passthrough/spec.md (AC8, AC12, AC14, AC15, AC16, AC20, AC21, AC22)
ADR: docs/decisions/0003-reverseproxy-with-rewrite-as-proxy-engine.md
Research: Q5 (ReverseProxy's pre-Rewrite changes), Q9 (ProxyFromEnvironment), Q16 (new: Proxy-* and re-added Upgrade)
Why this approach: Rewrite follows plan steps 1-5 (prefix off Path and RawPath, SetURL, RawQuery restored, client forwarding headers restored unless Connection lists them, Te deleted). Building it showed ReverseProxy leaves Proxy-* headers other than the two it knows, and re-adds Connection/Upgrade for a protocol switch, both hop-by-hop in the spec; step 5 now deletes those too and a minimal ModifyResponse strips Proxy-* on the response, since AC14 checks both directions (plan.md and research Q16 updated). ServeHTTP fills Meta.Protocol, Client and Auth when a Meta is in the context.
Alternatives rejected: cloning http.DefaultTransport (a test can replace it); relying on ReverseProxy's own hop-by-hop list (misses Proxy-*, re-adds Upgrade).
Trade-off / known limit: the gateway never switches protocols (no WebSocket through it). NewProxy takes the logger but does not use it yet: ErrorLog and the ErrorHandler land in T10, so until then a transport error goes through ReverseProxy's default handler. TestProxy_FillsMeta is an extra test beyond the task's eight.
Verified by: the eight named tests plus TestProxy_FillsMeta first failed to build (undefined: core.NewProxy), then pass under -race; temporary mutations each failed a test and were reverted: no RawQuery restore, no forwarding-header restore, ignoring Connection-listed forwarding headers, no Te/Upgrade/Proxy-* delete (request and response), DisableCompression off, SetXForwarded added, RawPath not stripped, Auth not filled; make verify.
